@cubic-dev-ai The overlap is intended, and I'd keep both. They answer different questions. Code Quality's job runs only the packages a PR changes and finishes in about four minutes, so it is the fast signal and its summary shows just those packages. This workflow runs every package against its minimums, which is the only place a change in one package that lowers another package's coverage gets caught, and it is the one that also runs on pushes to `main`.

Dropping the PR trigger here would lose that whole-repo gate before merge. Dropping the Code Quality job is what an earlier revision of this PR did, and it was reverted to keep Code Quality unchanged from #8600 (see the description). The shared work is small in practice: both runs use the Turbo remote cache for builds.

Are you fine leaving it as is?

@cubic-dev-ai I'd rather keep `&&` here. The job's result is the same either way: a Vitest or threshold failure already fails this task and the workflow, and `--continue` still runs every other workspace. The only thing the suggestion adds is the `node --test` output on a run that is already red, and the next run shows it once Vitest passes.

